stereo-declare (1.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: child windows of an X11 window. stereo_declare_x11_child() declares
    the child that holds the stereo content (the OpenGL area of a program
    whose interface is 2D), lists it once in the parent's
    _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_CHILDREN, and, for a child that holds both
    views at full width, writes its _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_ONE_VIEW_SIZE
    (support version 8), so the compositor shows each view at the full width
    of the child instead of stretching halves. stereo_remove_x11_child()
    gives the child back to the parent window.
  * New: stereo_declare_x11_child_place() sets the independent rectangle and
    the stacking below the parent's own surface of a listed child
    (_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_CHILD_PLACE, CHILD-PLACE.md), for a video
    that keeps its native raster under controls the ordinary window paints.
    Both are version 8 of the declaration.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300

stereo-declare (1.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: the X11 one-view place negotiation, version 7 of the stereo content
    declaration. stereo_x11_one_view_event() reads the place the window
    manager proposes (_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_ONE_VIEW_CONFIGURE: serial,
    width, height of one view) and stereo_declare_x11_one_view_commit()
    answers it after the program has rendered, so the window's place on
    screen follows the program instead of being stretched.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:20:00 -0300

stereo-declare (1.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: desktop depth, with version 3 of kde_stereo_content_manager_v1.
    stereo_depth_wayland_watch() follows a surface's depth state, whether
    its elements may be shown in depth now (it is on a stereo output and
    awake, not lying flat behind the active window) and which of its edges
    lie on its output's edge; stereo_depth_wayland_set_desktop_depth()
    marks the pair a toolkit draws once per eye as the desktop's own depth,
    not stereo content; stereo_depth_wayland_set_place() and
    stereo_depth_wayland_unset_place() declare where a popup surface sits,
    from -1 (the sunk limit) to 1 (the popped limit);
    stereo_depth_supported_wayland() says whether the compositor follows
    desktop depth. Without version 3 the calls return -ENOTSUP and a
    surface is never awake.
  * The library binds version 3 when the compositor offers it and carries
    the plasma-wayland-protocols fork's version 3 of the protocol file.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:30:43 -0300

stereo-declare (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: stereo_declare_x11_one_view_size(), the size one view is shown at
    for an X11 window whose views have another resolution, written as
    _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_ONE_VIEW_SIZE (KWin support version 6). The
    two 1920x540 views of a half top-and-bottom 1920x1080 video stay in a
    3840x540 window shown at 1920x1080, and the compositor resizes them
    once. stereo_remove_x11() removes it with the rest, and stereo_declare.py
    takes it as Declaration(one_view_size=...).
  * Wayland: the library binds kde-stereo-content-v1 at version 2 when the
    compositor offers it (a declared surface without a viewport destination
    is one view wide), and carries the protocol file as Stereo KWin does.
  * Package descriptions: each eye at the resolution it has.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:33:34 -0300

stereo-declare (1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Documentation: full side by side is the layout, the two eyes next to
    each other, left eye first, each at the resolution it has (a half
    top-and-bottom 1920x1080 frame is one 3840x540 picture); the size an
    eye is shown at is the surface's, and the compositor resizes once. The
    header, README, API.md and the Wayland example say so. The C library
    and the Python module are unchanged.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:48:38 -0300

stereo-declare (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: Declaration.windows_of() in stereo_declare.py, the one top-level
    window of a set of processes, for a program that draws full side by side
    itself and so has no state file. The C library is unchanged.

